    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6b445ef0-1a8c-4bb8-bd2e-c0d46943349d\n\n### Reproduction\n\ntesting config (for accountability purposes, this was generated by ai but still reviewed and tested by me)\n\n```lua\nvim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noselect'\nvim.o.swapfile = false\n\n-- Bootstrap latest mini.nvim into this isolated data dir\nlocal path_package = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/'\nlocal mini_path = path_package .. 'pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(mini_path) then\n  vim.fn.system({\n    'git', 'clone', '--filter=blob:none',\n    'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path,\n  })\n  vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL')\nend\n\nrequire('mini.snippets').setup({\n  snippets = {\n    { prefix = 'p', body = '\"${1:id}\": ${2:title}' },\n  },\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimEnter', {\n  once = true,\n  callback = function()\n    print([[\n=== mini.snippets <C-n> repro ===\n1. Press i to enter insert mode\n2. Type: p\n3. Press <C-j> to expand -> buffer becomes:  \"id\": \"\"\n4. Cursor sits on tabstop $1 (placeholder \"id\")\n5. Press <C-n>\n\nExpected: \"id\": \"\" unchanged (completion opens or no-ops)\nBug:      leading \" before id is deleted ->  id\": \"\"\n\nThis clone is mini.nvim's latest main, so this also checks\nwhether updating mini.nvim fixes the issue.\n]])\n  end,\n})\n```",
