            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@echasnovski,\n\nAlthough the title mentions `<C-n>` as  \"navigating backwards\", this issue can be reproduced with default `mini.snippets`. \n\nThe behavior occurs if the user navigates to the next tabstop, and immediately presses `<C-n>` expecting builtin `:h compl-keyword`. \nNote that the completion does work when the user first enters a character before pressing `<C-n>`.\n",
