        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The behavior occurs if the user navigates to the next tabstop, and immediately presses `<C-n>` expecting builtin `:h compl-keyword`.\n> Note that the completion does work when the user first enters a character before pressing `<C-n>`.\n\nYeah, I can reproduce. I am still hesitant to touch this part (interaction with built-in completion) of the 'mini.snippets' as it is very fragile (so much so that it deserved a not-so-small [dedicated test set](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/a59a9b7fb0a42cbcf022938ee5f0724320b66f63/tests/test_snippets.lua#L4691)).\n\nThe following solution that you suggested on Matrix seems to indeed not break tests, but I have a feeling that it can result in unexpected problems:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/snippets.lua b/lua/mini/snippets.lua\nindex 44bbc98f..3907deca 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/snippets.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/snippets.lua\n@@ -2773,15 +2773,15 @@ H.ensure_cur_buf = function(buf_id)\n end\n \n H.set_cursor = function(pos)\n+  -- NOTE: This won't put cursor past enf of line (for cursor in Insert mode to\n+  -- append text to the line). Ensure that Insert mode is active prior.\n+  vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, pos)\n+\n   -- Ensure no built-in completion window\n   -- HACK: Always clearing (and not *only* when pumvisible) accounts for weird\n   -- edge case when it is not visible (i.e. candidates *just* got exhausted)\n   -- but will still \"clear and restore\" text leading to squashing of extmarks.\n   H.hide_completion()\n-\n-  -- NOTE: This won't put cursor past enf of line (for cursor in Insert mode to\n-  -- append text to the line). Ensure that Insert mode is active prior.\n-  vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, pos)\n end\n \n H.call_in_insert_mode = function(f)\n```\n\nI'll maybe test drive it until the planned 0.18.0 release. If I forget about it after the release, could you please remind me about this?",
